From 70d4d352ae8e046f9ebfa993bd9d04a84bd8136e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Medium1992 <Medium1992@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 23:16:32 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 84/84] XHTTP: Grow the downloads of a connection at their mean
 rate

pi stepped each download's cap up and down in proportion to its own
rate, so two downloads of one connection kept whatever split they
started with: a second download started 5 s after the first took 0.74
of a 50 Mbit/s link with a 50 ms round trip, against 0.51 without the
governor. A step up is now taken at the mean rate of the connection's
downloads that their caps hold; steps down stay each one's own. The
steps add up as before, so the queue sees the same loop, and a single
download moves as it did. The same stand gives 0.63.
---
